 { By a 'bridge' I refer to the idea of covering the king with a fellow piece, usually a rook or a bishop, thus cutting the range of an enemy piece. We have already seen many cases of such bridges (by the way, 'curtains' is another possible expression) in earlier examples, for example Lucena's bridge at the beginning of the present chapter. Here are a few further examples. }  
 *

