1... { -KEY- } Rd6 $1 { Before pushing the pawn Black should create a bridge on the d-file. } ( { Instead, the game went } 1... e2 $2 2. Ra1 Kd2 3. Ra2 Kd3 4. Ra3 Kd4 5. Ra4 Kc3 6. Ra3 { and White's side attack saved a draw. } ) 
2. Kf3 ( { Obviously, } 2. Ra1 { made no sense, because of } Rd1 { followed by ...e3-e2, when a side attack is no longer available for White. } ) 
e2 3. Ra1+ Rd1 4. Ra2 Rd3+ 5. Kg2 Rd8 $1 { A timely switch of angle, creating the threat of 6... Rg8+, followed by ...Kf1. } 6. Ra1+ ( { Or } 6. Kf3 Kf1 $1 { , and taking on e2 costs White the rook. } ) 
Kd2 7. Ra2+ Ke3 8. Ra3+ Rd3 $1 { The bridge. } 9. Ra1 Rd1 { Black wins - White's side checks can be met by simply approaching the King to the White Rook. } 
