 { Without the a-pawn, White would win mechanically by Ra1-d1-d4(d5), creating Lucena's bridge. whereas here he must proceed with more accuracy. } 1. { -KEY- } Ra5 $1 { Losing a tempo. } ( { a) } 1. Ra8 Kd7 2. Ra6 { also does the trick; } ) 
 ( { b) but } 1. Ra6 $2 Kd7 { leads to mutual zugzwang; e.g. } 2. Ra5 Rf4 { and a bridge on the fifth rank won't work: } 3. Kg7 Rg4 4. Kf6 Rf4 5. Rf5 $4 Rxf5 6. Kxf5 Ke7 ) 
Kd7 2. Ra6 $1 { Zugzwang: if the black rook leaves the g-file then 3.Kg7 with a bridge on the sixth rank decides, while abandoning the fourth rank costs the a-pawn. } Kd8 3. Rd6+ Kc7 4. Ke7 ( { Seeing that } 4. Ke7 Rf4 { runs into } 5. Rf6 Re4 6. Re6 { with a decisive bridge, Black resigned. } ) 

 1-0

