 { It is clear that White will have to sacrifice the rook for the b-pawn, but which is the right way to do it? } 1. { -KEY- } Rb5 $2 ( { The intermediate check } 1. Rc5 $1 { was called for; e.g. } Kb4 ( { or } 1. Rb5 Kd3 2. Rb5 Kc4 3. Rb8 b2 4. Ke4 { with similar play; } ) 
2. Rc1 b2 3. Rb1 Kc3 4. Ke4 $1 { king first; } ( { in contrast, } 4. f5 $2 { runs into } Ra4 $1 { decisively cutting the king off; } ) 
Ra1 5. Rxb2 Kxb2 6. f5 { with a draw - Baburin. } ) 
b2 ( { The immediate } 1... Ra4 { also works, for example, } 2. Kg4 b2 { transposing to the mainline. } ) 
2. Kg4 ( { Perhaps only at this point White discovered that } 2. Ke4 $2 { runs into } Ra4 $1 3. Ke5 Rb4 ) 
Ra4 $1 { The threat of building a bridge on b4 forces White to sacrifices his rook much earlier than desired. } 3. Rxb2 Kxb2 4. Kg5 Kc3 5. f5 Kd4 6. f6 Ke5 
